# Research Companion - sample environment configuration
#
# Copy to `.env` and fill in real values (`.env` is gitignored - never commit secrets).
# NOTE: the app reads plain environment variables; it does NOT auto-load .env files.
#   PowerShell:  Get-Content .env | ForEach-Object { $n,$v = $_ -split '=',2; if ($n -and $n -notmatch '^#') { Set-Item "env:$n" $v } }
#   bash/zsh:    set -a; source .env; set +a
#   or persist on Windows:  setx OPENAI_API_KEY "sk-..."   (new shells only)

# --- LLM provider (need ONE of the two keys) --------------------------------

# OpenAI (used when RESEARCH_COMPANION_PROVIDER=openai)
OPENAI_API_KEY=sk-proj-your-openai-key-here

# Anthropic (the default provider)
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-your-anthropic-key-here

# Which provider the agent lanes use for their default LLM calls:
#   anthropic (default) | openai
RESEARCH_COMPANION_PROVIDER=openai

# Optional model override (otherwise a sensible per-provider default is used,
# e.g. gpt-4o for openai). Examples: gpt-4o-2024-11-20, gpt-4o-mini
# RESEARCH_COMPANION_MODEL=gpt-4o-2024-11-20

# --- Storage -----------------------------------------------------------------

# Where papers, extractions, the graph, and run audit logs live.
# Default: ~/.research-companion
# RESEARCH_COMPANION_DIR=C:\Users\you\.research-companion

# --- Notes ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# * `review --fast`, `refcheck`, and `examples/demo_offline.py` need NO key at all.
# * `build`, full `review` (novelty lane), and `rebuttal` make LLM calls:
#   pass --provider openai to `build`/`chat` explicitly, or rely on the vars above
#   for the agent lanes.
# * Scholarly lookups (CrossRef, OpenAlex, Semantic Scholar, arXiv) are free, no key.
